%% Figure 3: Core Business Sequence Diagram - End-to-End Wrong-Answer Troubleshooting (Sequence Diagram: Diagnose)
%% JC2001 Group 5 / Smart Study Assistant
%% Notes:
%%   1. Participants and core contracts align with the current FastAPI modular service architecture: POST /api/diagnose
%%      (receives question_id and selected_option); POST /api/tutor is an optional planned extension.
%%   2. The alt branches in the figure are exactly NFR-02 "Offline Reliability": both the external graph and the external model are optional,
%%      and when either is unavailable the core flow still returns results from local curated content.
%%   3. Labels [Implemented] = already landed in backend/app and frontend/app.js and passing tests;
%%      [Planned] = design target, not yet connected to real external services; [Optional] = injected via environment variables.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as University Student
    participant UI as Frontend Console (app.js)
    participant API as Business Hub (backend/app)
    participant Store as Question Bank and Knowledge Base (seed_questions.py)
    participant Graph as Neo4j Graph (Cloud)
    participant Qwen as Qwen Qwen-Turbo

    User->>UI: Click a question distractor (e.g., option B)
    UI->>API: POST /api/diagnose {question_id, selected_option}
    API->>Store: Read stem, correct answer, and trap mapping [Implemented]
    Store-->>API: trap_id, misconception, prerequisite
    Note over API,Store: Answer and misconception mapping is not exposed via the public client question API
    API->>API: evaluate_answer determines is_correct=false
    alt External graph available [Planned]
        API->>Graph: MATCH (q:Question)-[:PRONE_TO]->(t:Trap)
        Graph-->>API: Knowledge point names, predecessor concepts, and trigger labels
    else Graph miss or timeout [Degraded]
        API->>API: Degrade to local curated misconception topology and prerequisite knowledge
    end
    API-->>UI: 200 OK (DiagnoseResponse: {is_correct, trap, socratic_hint, prerequisite, radar_updates})
    UI->>UI: Expand the right-side diagnosis drawer and highlight the corresponding option
    UI-->>User: Show Socratic guiding prompts, prerequisite concepts, and pitfall-avoidance advice
    opt Student continues multi-turn follow-up [Planned - Tutor Follow-up Extension]
        User->>UI: Enter a follow-up question in the dialogue drawer
        UI->>API: POST /api/tutor {question_id, message}
        alt External model configured [Optional]
            API->>Qwen: Compatible-protocol request /chat/completions
            Qwen-->>API: Return a deeply eliciting follow-up reply
        else Model not configured or call timed out [Local Degradation]
            API->>API: local_tutor_reply generated from the reviewed evidence chain
        end
        API-->>UI: 200 OK {reply, mode}
        UI-->>User: Show the tutor reply with source annotation
    end
    UI->>UI: Append the answer record to localStorage
    UI-->>User: Refresh the learning-mastery radar and dimension pass status
